6. What This Framework Proves and DOES NOT Prove
What it PROVES:

That modular projections with gcd(q,m)=1 destroy the observed statistical noise structure in LWE and ML-KEM.

That real transformations of compression, rounding, and serialization in Kyber preserve high uniformity and provide no statistical advantage to an attacker.

What it DOES NOT Prove:

A breakdown of the cryptographic security of ML-KEM / Kyber (FIPS 203).

Physical side-channel vulnerabilities (SPA/DPA) outside the statistical data model.

